"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The surgical findings included a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pT3a stage with extraprostatic extension, but negative surgical margins and no seminal vesicle invasion were noted. The absence of lymph nodes removed, indicated by \"no lymph nodes were removed,\" widens uncertainty regarding nodal status, as pNx is not equivalent to pN0. The biopsy showed Acinar adenocarcinoma with perineural invasion.\n\nCountervailing factors include the negative surgical margins and absence of lymphovascular invasion. The preoperative PSA was 6. The primary uncertainty lies in the missing postoperative PSA and subsequent trajectory, which is critical for monitoring disease progression. Information regarding the biopsy-to-prostatectomy differences is documented, but the lack of previous notes prevents a complete assessment of the patient's history. Postoperative PSA levels and their trajectory would significantly revise this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 58.61 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 35.17–82.06 months; its coverage has not been validated."
